uniTube — attribution and provenance
====================================

uniTube itself is BSD-2-Clause, Copyright (c) 2026 Cameron Brooks. That covers
everything under src/, examples/, tests/, tools/, checks/, docs/ and spikes/,
plus the build files at the root. It has NO third-party dependencies and links
to nothing, so USING uniTube carries no obligation beyond BSD-2-Clause.

The only third-party code in this repository is under reference/, which no part
of uniTube imports, links to, or is derived from. It is present as prior art and
is MERELY AGGREGATED here in the sense of GPLv3 section 5 -- separate works, on a
shared volume, not a combined work. Their licences are below.

Everything under reference/ is READ-ONLY QUARANTINE. It is retained as prior
art, as a requirements checklist, and as the historical record of what this
project grew out of. No file under src/ may import from reference/ — this is
enforced by `just lint` and stated in AGENTS.md.


